# ForgeLoop Cursor Rules

Use these rules when working in this repository with Cursor Agent.

## Workflow

- Follow Discover, Frame, Build, Check, Capture for non-trivial work.
- Inspect before editing.
- Keep changes small and reversible.
- Update docs when behaviour changes.
- Capture reusable lessons after meaningful work.

## Token Economy

Before reading broad memory folders, run:

```bash
python -m forgeloop pack "<task query>" . --limit 5
```

Use the FCP/1 output as a pointer list.

Open only exact source files that matter for the current task.

Do not paste whole memory folders into chat.

## Validation

Run relevant checks before calling work complete:

```bash
python -m unittest discover -s tests
python -m forgeloop validate .
python -m forgeloop compat .
python -m forgeloop index . --check
python -m forgeloop secrets check .
```

## Safety

- Keep secrets outside the repository.
- Do not add active hooks without review and tests.
- Do not edit generated memory indexes manually.
- Do not make percentage token-savings claims without measured output.
